Design a production-grade distributed Version Control System similar to GitHub.

Requirements:

- Support 100 million repositories.
- Support 10 million daily active developers.
- Allow concurrent commits from multiple contributors.
- Support branching, merging, rebasing, pull requests, code reviews, and repository forking.
- Store complete commit history efficiently.
- Support repositories larger than 50 GB.
- Provide near real-time search across all repositories.
- Support role-based access control for organizations and private repositories.
- Generate webhooks for repository events.
- Support Git over HTTPS and SSH.
- Handle large binary files efficiently.
- Provide high availability across multiple regions.
- Ensure no commit is lost during failures.
- Repository cloning should remain performant even for very large repositories.
- The system should tolerate regional outages.
- Minimize storage costs using deduplication where appropriate.

The design should be production-ready and explicitly justify every major architectural decision.